 "says": "Alice has selected no Instructions at all: her personal preparation request pins no source. She opens a link to her host session and composes the session's start from that request; the owner returns a preparation that holds no unit and records the session as selected only. She then activates the session with that preparation. The routing the owner returns is activated, carries no projection, and still carries the memory usage contract - the short text the runtime writes and a guide pointer naming the guide's path and the digest of the guide bytes this installation holds. The always surface is unchanged and native instruction files are preserved. Observing the session shows it activated with nothing delivered, for the link it was started on. Zero selected Instructions must not stop activation or drop the usage contract, and activation must not add to the always surface or write a native file.",
 "spec_sha256": "4c6067e5468eeb08233d2032e11818b666568c0229659b7f55dbf9ed26cf53de",
